  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef is watching a movie, and during the intermission, wants to get himself some snacks.\n\nA bucket of popcorn costs XXX rupees, and a drink costs YYY rupees.\n\nThere is also a combo offer available, which provides one bucket of popcorn and one drink at a cost of ZZZ rupees.\n\nChef wants to buy two buckets of popcorn and three drinks.\n\nWhat's the **minimum** amount he needs to pay to do so?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input will contain three space-separated integers X,Y,X, Y, X,Y, and ZZZ — the price of one bucket of popcorn, one drink, and the combo, respectively.\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint a single integer: the minimum price Chef needs to pay to buy two buckets of popcorn and three drinks.",
    "constraints": [
      "50≤X,Y,Z≤20050 \\leq X, Y, Z \\leq 20050≤X,Y,Z≤200",
      "X,Y≤ZX, Y \\le ZX,Y≤Z"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "100 70 160",
        "output": "390",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nWe can use 222 combo offers for 160160160 each and then a drink for 707070, totalling 390390390."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "110 80 200",
        "output": "460",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nIt is optimal to buy all the 222 popcorns and 333 drinks individually for 2⋅110+3⋅80=4602 \\cdot 110 + 3 \\cdot 80 = 4602⋅110+3⋅80=460."
      }
    ]
  },
